~/.config/themes/ -- desktop themes
====================================

One folder per theme. Switch with any of:
    ~/.config/hypr/scripts/theme.py set <name>     (or display.py theme <name>)
    the THEME chips in the display panel (SUPER+ALT+D)
    "Theme: <name>" in the launcher's command palette (ALT+E, then ">")
The choice is theme=<name> in ~/.local/state/hypr/display.conf and survives
`hyprctl reload`, gamemode OFF and logins.

    cyberpunk/   the base: today's neon look. Every other theme inherits its
                 theme.conf keys; its stylesheets are empty because the base
                 files (waybar/style.css...) ARE cyberpunk.
    matrix/      phosphor green on black, IBM Plex Mono everywhere, square
                 1px panes, fixed accent #00ff41 (amber warn, red bad);
                 wallpapers: ~/.config/hypr/scripts/make-matrix-wallpaper.py
                 --all (digital rain, matrix-1..4.png on all three monitors)
    aero/        Windows 7 Aero Glass: deep-blue frosted glass with a gloss
                 on the top half of every pill and card, 6-8px corners, soft
                 shadows, white text with a faint dark shadow, Selawik (the
                 open Segoe UI stand-in, ~/.local/share/fonts/themes/aero/,
                 README there: source + OFL) with IBM Plex Sans fallback;
                 accent follows the wallpaper but is always tempered into
                 Aero sky blue first (@a-tone, waybar.css header), so a
                 neon pick never shows raw; Nautilus as real frosted glass
                 (gtk4.css + hypr.lua). Wallpapers:
                 ~/.config/hypr/scripts/make-aero-wallpaper.py --all
                 (aero-{aurora,blue,harmony,teal,violet}.png, kept cool so
                 the accent never lands on the bad red or warn amber)
    win95/       Windows 95: opaque dimmed grey (#acacac, not #c0c0c0 --
                 HDR), real 3D bevels (inset box-shadows, border width 0),
                 square corners, navy selection under white text, status as
                 solid fills; the bar is a raised taskbar strip with the
                 clock in a sunken tray well and the focused title as the
                 pressed, dithered task button (dither.png); launcher and
                 wofi are the Start menu. W95FA at 12.5px, monochrome
                 (~/.local/share/fonts/themes/win95/, README there: source +
                 OFL; ~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/60-w95fa-pixels.conf turns
                 its antialiasing off), fixed navy accent, calm animations,
                 Nautilus in Windows 95 colours (gtk4.css). Wallpapers:
                 ~/.config/hypr/scripts/make-win95-wallpaper.py --all
                 (win95-teal plus win95-clouds-1..3, drawn from scratch)
    moe/         萌え: pastel sakura. Pink / lavender / peach GLASS bubbles
                 (dimmed for HDR: pills #e8c4d6, cards #dcb6c9) with deep
                 plum text, everything round, Rounded Mplus 1c + Hachi Maru
                 Pop (~/.local/share/fonts/themes/moe/README), lang=ja (the
                 day 10月18日 (日), workspaces 一 二 三, a Japanese launcher
                 prompt), the accent ROLE deep rose (text-safe; the sakura
                 pastel is set explicitly for fills and glows), Papirus with
                 pink folders (icon_theme=Moe), the Catppuccin pink cursor,
                 a sakura-night terminal with a kaomoji prompt, uosc pastel
                 + moe-hud.lua in mpv, sakura / Fuji / yozakura / kawaii
                 wallpapers (make-moe-wallpaper.py --all) and falling petals
                 (make-moe-sakura.py --all)
    icons        icon_theme= in theme.conf (gsettings icon-theme, live in
                 GTK apps; mako's icon-path): cyberpunk Adwaita, aero
                 oxygen (needs `sudo dnf install oxygen-icon-theme`; Adwaita
                 until then), matrix Phosphor, win95 Win95. Phosphor and
                 Win95 are BUILT, not installed:
                 ~/.config/hypr/scripts/make-icon-theme.py --all (rerun
                 after installing an app; --sheet <variant> shows a before/
                 after sheet). Win95 inherits Chicago95
                 (~/.local/share/icons/Chicago95/README: source, licence,
                 reinstall) and adds the apps it lacks, aliased to a
                 Chicago95 picture or put through the 16-colour filter
    tools/statebar.py      a test bar with every pill state, for screenshots
                           (`statebar.py shot FILE.png`; deterministic, so two
                           shots of one theme compare pixel for pixel)

A theme folder
--------------
    theme.conf    key=value; every key optional; cyberpunk/theme.conf lists
                  all of them with today's values and comments. font= and
                  font_mono= may be a list, first choice first
                  ("font=Selawik, IBM Plex Sans")
    waybar.css    bar + toolbox   (overrides waybar/style.css, style-toolbox.css)
    panel.css     popup panels    (overrides waybar/panel.css)
    launcher.css  launcher, quick note, clipboard (overrides hypr/scripts/launcher.css)
    llm-chat.css  the LLM chat window (overrides hypr/scripts/
                  llm-chat.css; an open window restyles itself on a
                  switch). Its mascot is per theme too, in code:
                  hypr/scripts/mascots.py (moe_mascot.py, mascot_<theme>.py;
                  `mascots.py --check` after changing one)
    wofi.css      wofi            (overrides wofi/style.css)
    mako          mako fragment   (key=value lines, may repeat [sections])
    gtk4.css      libadwaita / GTK4 (becomes ~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css;
                  :root { --window-bg-color: ...; --accent-bg-color: ...; })
                  read when a GTK4 app STARTS: Nautilus is one process for
                  all its windows. `theme.py set` restarts it when it has
                  no window open, else waits for the last one to close
                  (the toast offers "Restart Files now"); gsettings parts
                  change live
    hypr.lua      optional: return { window_rules = {...}, layer_rules = {...} }
                  enabled only while this theme is current (lua/display.lua)
Missing file = no override. After editing any of them: theme.py apply.
Before switching to a new theme: theme.py check <name>.

How the overrides work (the short version; theme.py's docstring and the
header of each base stylesheet have the long one): every base stylesheet
starts with a PALETTE of @define-color names and uses only those names in
its rules. The theme's css is imported LAST, after the wallpaper accent, and
GTK3 resolves a named colour by its LAST definition -- so redefining
`@define-color surface ...;` recolours every pill. Anything that is not a
colour (radius, border width, font size, padding) is changed by repeating the
base file's selector, which wins by coming later. font= / font_mono= in
theme.conf swap the face in every base rule automatically.

Rules every theme keeps
-----------------------
  * @cyan is the ACCENT role whatever its hue; set the theme's base accent
    with accent= in theme.conf rather than in css, so the wallpaper accent
    can still replace it when accent_follow=yes.
  * Status colours stay distinguishable: good (green, @good / @good-fg),
    warn (yellow, @warn / @warn-fg), bad (magenta-red, @bad / @bad-fg /
    @critical). DP-1 is HDR: large light areas must be dimmed (no
    full-white surfaces).
  * The bar stays at the top; nothing here moves it.
  * Panel sizes follow the theme's font. A narrower face (Selawik in aero,
    W95FA in win95) makes most panels a little smaller than in cyberpunk --
    aero measured disk 832x589 vs 861x628, display 432x507 vs 432x562 (its
    THEME chips fit one row), calendar 277x310 vs 286x330, audio 400x360
    vs 400x376; the CARD_HEIGHT=412 cards (CPU, GPU, network, updates,
    notifications) do not change. So check a panel layout change in more
    than one theme, and never take one theme's sizes as the reference.
